"""
Pipe time-synced lyrics to a file for use with GNOME Shell Executor
or the bundled GNOME top-bar extension.

Playback information is read directly from the local MPRIS D-Bus
interface, so no Spotify developer account, Client ID/Secret, or
login token is required.

Lyrics sources (in order):
  1. local .lrc folder from sptlrx's config (`local.folder`)
  2. NetEase Cloud Music (same public eapi endpoints used by Lyricify)
  3. LRCLIB (https://lrclib.net)

Single-threaded: no deadlocks, no GIL issues.

Usage: sptlrx-pipe [output_path]
  Default output path: /tmp/sptlrx-lyrics

Logs: /tmp/sptlrx-lyrics.log
"""

